.TH UNIQ 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
uniq \- report or omit repeated lines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uniq
[\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-d\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collapse adjacent matching lines of FILE (standard input by default) into one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Prefix each line with its number of occurrences.
.TP
.B \-d
Print only lines that had at least one duplicate.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
